  {
   "k": "g27872",
   "en": "The ⟦0⟧ attribute sets the anchor point of an element. As example, ⟦1⟧ sets ⟦2⟧ to be in the top left corner of the screen or container, and ⟦3⟧ sets it to be the bottom right instead.",
   "frags": 4
  },
  {
   "k": "1urojq6",
   "en": "orientation = UPPER_LEFT"
  },
  {
   "k": "iz23as",
   "en": "position = { x = 0 y = 0 }"
  },
  {
   "k": "1sa24ce",
   "en": "orientation = LOWER_RIGHT"
  },
  {
   "k": "1y2pmm2",
   "en": "The ⟦0⟧ attribute sets the position of an element relatively to its orientation. For example, ⟦1⟧ with ⟦2⟧ will result in the element being 120 pixels to the right and 100 pixels to the bottom relatively to the upper left corner of its container, while ⟦3⟧ will result in it being 120 pixels to the left and 100 pixels to the top from the lower right corner.",
   "frags": 4
  },
  {
   "k": "1gvq5di",
   "en": "position = { x = 120 y = 100 }"
  },
